 ebsite: https://2026.acmmm.org/\nSource URL: https://2026.acmmm.org/site/
 important-dates.html\nLocation: Rio de Janeiro\, Brazil\nTopics: Multimed
 ia Learning & Retrieval\, Computer Vision & Pattern Recognition\, Deep Re
 presentation Learning\, Signal Processing\nSize: XL\nSubmission type: Pap
 er-based / multimedia research\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date:
  2026-10-07\nNotes: Official 2026 pages confirm Rio and deadline days. Th
 e retrieved important-dates page has no cutoff hour or timezone\, so the 
 stored AoE timestamps are provisional. Main\, BNI\, and dataset tracks sh
 are March/April deadlines\; workshop papers have their own route. XL is a
 n editorial estimate.\nScope: Multimedia understanding\, learning\, gener
 ation\, and retrieval across image\, video\, audio\, language\, and other
  modalities. Characteristic work includes multimodal fusion\, generative 
 and foundation models\, scalable indexing and search\, cross-modal alignm
 ent\, and human-centered multimedia experiences. The 2026 steering-commit
 tee scope also emphasizes explainability. Healthcare\, education\, and en
 tertainment are applications\, not blanket topical identities.\nAdditiona
 l topics: Machine Learning\, Natural Language Processing & LLMs\, Human-A
 I Interaction & Deployment\, Data Mining & Data Science\, Explainability 
 & Interpretability\nScope sources (2026): https://2026.acmmm.org/site/top
 ics.html\, https://2026.acmmm.org/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07\nOffic
